Subject: d3d11: defer On12 driver allocation until backend work is requested

Unity's D3D12 path can create an On12 frontend only to identify its DXGI
adapter. Opening DTL at that point reserves heaps for a device that never
submits D3D11 work. Preserve the frontend and controlling identity, validate
caller inputs through an allocation-free core export, and open the adapter
once on first backend use. Keep initialization failures terminal and visible
through GetDeviceRemovedReason. Empty ClearState and unused teardown have no
driver state to reset. Ordinary WineD3D paths retain their dispatch.

Requires WineD3D11On12ValidateDeviceV1 (ordinal 45). Applies after patches
0001-0026 to WineCX 7dbc5b5322a6ef3fb04bdc643c64b188fd641149.

